  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $P=\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right)$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} P^{2} &=P \\cdot P=\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right)\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}4+2-4 & -4-6+8 & -8 & -8+12 \\\\ -2-3+4 & 2+9-8 & 4+12-12 \\\\ 2+2-3 & -2-6+6 & -4-8+9\\end{array}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(\\begin{array}{ccc}2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{array}\\right)=P \\\\ \\therefore P^{4}=P^{2}=P \\\\ \\Rightarrow P^{5}=P^{2}=P \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
